WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.860
- Hello to you Rasputin.

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.550
Give my regards to the czar.

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:04.749
- I will relay the message.

00:00:04.749 --> 00:00:07.590
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:10.040
- Oh, I don't know why I
thought I could do this.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:13.180
I'm drowning, and cats hate drowning.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:14.900
- If I may, I believe I can take on

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.360
more responsibility around here,

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.180
on a provisional basis of course.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.013
- Okay.

00:00:19.013 --> 00:00:22.340
- But we're small agency and
we need to think like one.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:23.770
Instead of us spreading ourselves thinner

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:25.510
we should be focusing
on getting better gigs

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:27.147
for the clients we already have.

00:00:27.147 --> 00:00:29.240
- Oh, like Jerry Maguire.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.730
- Yes.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.890
What part of Jerry Maguire?

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:35.140
- The part where Tom Cruise's
agent got him a massive payday

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:36.900
for being in Jerry Maguire.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.780
(upbeat music)

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:39.890
Okay, looking good.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:40.850
Fantastic.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:41.750
You need a coaster.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.280
I told you to wear lipstick
and underpants, Theresa.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.930
- I put everything
bill-related in one folder.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.150
- Great.
- Gas bill, cable bill

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:48.890
and the new headshots for Bill-E-Zane.

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:49.723
- Thank you Judah.

00:00:49.723 --> 00:00:51.840
You also wanted me to remind
you to call Mr. Peanut Butter.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:52.673
Yeah, thank you.

00:00:52.673 --> 00:00:54.760
Ping me again in two
minutes, no five minutes.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.520
When's our call with
BoJack Ana Spanakopita?

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.110
- You mean the one that
started seven minutes ago?

00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:59.420
It started seven minutes ago.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:00.253
- What?

00:01:00.253 --> 00:01:02.500
- Diane's in your office
right now stalling, poorly.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.570
I settled on a company dental plan.

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:06.060
It's called the tooth, the whole tooth

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.080
and nothing but the tooth.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:07.913
Seemed comprehensive.

00:01:07.913 --> 00:01:11.120
- Not too thabby Judah. (chuckling)

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.140
- Yes.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:14.680
I also wanted to talk to
you, if this is a good time,

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:16.550
and it is because you
have exactly nine minutes

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.460
before your meeting on Captain Hooker Two,

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.150
Yo Hoe Hoe and a Bottle of Booty.

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:20.983
- Yeah, what's up?

00:01:20.983 --> 00:01:22.260
- As you know I've taken on duties

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.380
beyond the scope of my original contract.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:25.477
I think I've proven my work.

00:01:25.477 --> 00:01:27.220
- Are you asking for a raise?

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.940
- A more elegant solution might involve

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.650
an ownership position in the company.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.420
I thought I'd ask you for 15% stake,

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.250
you counter with five
and then we settle on 10.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:35.570
- Well then, it's settled.

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:36.560
- I'll draw up the paperwork.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.740
Speaking of paper, Piper
Perabo and Pauley Perrette

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:39.770
need to push back the pitch on

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:41.070
the Princess and the Pauper project.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:42.150
So you have a night off tonight.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:42.983
- A night off?

00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:44.300
When's the last time that happened?

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.133
- It hasn't.

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:45.966
Can I help you with anything else?

00:01:45.966 --> 00:01:47.540
Yeah, you can give me a date for tonight.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.160
Actually, make that three dates.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:51.400
Who knows when I'm gonna
get another night off.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.318
- I do, and you won't.

00:01:53.318 --> 00:01:54.250
(sighing)

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:55.740
Princess Caroline, I made reservations

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:56.970
for you tonight at Elefante.

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:57.890
- Reservations?

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:58.723
For your dates.

00:01:58.723 --> 00:02:00.620
You have one a seven, one
at 8:30 and one at 10.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.240
- You actually got me three dates?

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:03.260
I was joking.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:05.260
- I'm sorry, I sometimes
have trouble reading tone.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:07.510
One time I spent 45 minutes
at a fascinating lecture

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:09.130
at the Apollo Theater before I realized

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:10.100
it was a comedy routine.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.230
- Well, I can't go on three days.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:13.860
Can we reschedule two of them?

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.730
- It's going to be a
long time before you get

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:17.540
another night off,
especially since you have

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:18.780
all those lawyers coming next week

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:19.950
to change the light bulbs.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:23.045
Okay, I just realized
now that was also a joke.

00:02:23.045 --> 00:02:25.920
(light music)

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.310
Oh, why were you working in the dark?

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:30.210
- Oh, I guess it got dark.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.220
I didn't notice.

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:32.170
How were your dates?

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:33.830
- Oh, pointless.

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:34.956
- Yes, most dates are.

00:02:34.956 --> 00:02:35.789
- Ha!

00:02:35.789 --> 00:02:36.810
- Well, I prepared our agreement.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.325
Look it over and sign it at your leisure.

00:02:38.325 --> 00:02:39.840
- I don't have any leisure.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:40.770
- While you're signing things,

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:42.460
I have a stack of holiday
cards for the staff.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:44.830
I took the liberty of writing
little personal messages

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:46.040
to everyone on your behalf.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:46.873
- Thank you.

00:02:46.873 --> 00:02:47.706
- Uh huh.

00:02:49.761 --> 00:02:52.261
(light music)

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:05.200
- Hey man, loved you in
The Caveman's Valentine.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.033
- Huh?

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:06.921
- Nothing?

00:03:06.921 --> 00:03:07.754
The Caveman's Valentine.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:09.730
Samuel L. Jackson had that big beard.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:10.563
Look it up.

00:03:10.563 --> 00:03:11.410
When you start laughing, call me.

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:12.243
- Will do.

00:03:12.243 --> 00:03:13.210
Vanessa, Gecko on line two.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.220
- Great, put that raggedy-ass bitch on.

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:17.770
I'm gonna bash her around
like a ball of foil.

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:19.830
- I know you're excited but we are still

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:21.400
in a very precarious position,

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.854
and I wonder if foil ball
batting is the best tack here.

00:03:24.854 --> 00:03:27.290
(downtrodden music)

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:28.204
- Oh good, you're still here.

00:03:28.204 --> 00:03:30.378
I wanted to get a head
start on the 2016 budget.

00:03:30.378 --> 00:03:31.211
- Oh.

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:32.044
- It's going to be a challenge

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:33.300
but assuming BoJack books Pegasus.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:34.990
BoJack didn't book Pegasus.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.412
- Oh so he's doing the Jelly Bean Movie?

00:03:36.412 --> 00:03:38.020
- No, that fell apart, too.

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:40.020
- Well then, we're
gonna have to cut costs.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.300
Our social media division strikes me

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.760
as a luxury we can no longer afford,

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:44.410
but if things don't perk
up in the first quarter,

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:46.070
we might be looking at broader layoffs.

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:48.100
- Jesus Christ, Judah,
do you ever read a room?

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.790
- I'm sorry, is this a bad time?

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:52.050
- Is midnight on New Years, a bad time?

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:52.905
I don't know.

00:03:52.905 --> 00:03:55.930
Why don't you run that through
your robot analysis protocol

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:57.820
and get back to me once
you've assessed the data.

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.330
- I am not a robot, I am a human being.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.410
- You want to make some cuts?

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:03.370
Why don't you cut that stupid beard.

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:05.260
Everyone who walks in
here thinks this place

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:06.665
is run by a homeless person.

00:04:06.665 --> 00:04:08.450
- I apologize if my appearance

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:09.793
or demeanor is unprofessional.

00:04:09.793 --> 00:04:12.810
- (sighing) No, you're perfect.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:15.370
Everybody's perfect except for me.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:16.320
Just go home Judah.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:17.920
- Would you like me to
shave the beard or--

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:19.756
- Just go home Judah.

00:04:19.756 --> 00:04:21.250
(fireworks crackle)

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:22.668
- Happy New Year, Princess Caroline.

00:04:22.668 --> 00:04:25.530
(downtrodden music)

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:27.570
As a partner in the company,
I am prepared to forgo

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:28.920
my salary for the next three months

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:31.590
but even then we're going to
need some sort of miracle.

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:32.890
- What are we doing?

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:34.400
What was the point of any of this?

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:37.010
I wasted everyone's time for six months.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:40.040
Soon I'll get some offer from
one of the big five agencies

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:42.050
that I can't say no to and I'll go back

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:44.100
to being another cog in the giant Plate

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:46.700
'O Spaghetti Maker that is this industry.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.107
Is that the best I can hope for?

00:04:48.107 --> 00:04:49.060
- Not necessarily.

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:51.910
Although there was one thing
I should probably mention.

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:52.933
- What is it, Judah?

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.640
- Maybe this is an opportunity

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:58.942
to live one of your other eight lives.

00:04:58.942 --> 00:05:01.710
- Yeah, maybe.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.110
It's been a pleasure
working with you, Judah.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:06.140
- I found it to be an
above average experience.

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:08.523
Please forgive me for getting emotional.

00:05:08.523 --> 00:05:09.560
- Oh my god.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:10.690
Thank God you're not a mother,

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:13.090
you would be hilarious at it.

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:14.930
Hey, today was fun.

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:17.340
I'll call you in the morning
we'll figure this out.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:18.290
We'll deal with it.

00:05:19.325 --> 00:05:20.760
(heavy sighing)

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:22.120
- If you'd like to never see him again,

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.690
I have ways of getting rid of him.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:25.420
- What kind of ways?

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.520
- Asking him politely to not come back.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:28.900
Actually that's only one way.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:31.220
I apologize for misleading
you about the number of ways.

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:32.230
- He's a jerk right?

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:33.140
It's not just me?

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:34.650
- I've worked with guys like him in FME.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:36.440
And when I left, I
swore I would never work

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.100
at a big agency again because

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.870
I can't work with people like that.

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:41.070
- You don't think I'm like that?

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.730
- No because you care about
people other than yourself.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:46.610
And for what it's worth, you
will be a wonderful mother.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:47.870
- You're not just saying that?

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:49.320
- I never just say anything.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:50.560
I choose my words very carefully

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:52.910
with an eye towards
precision and expediency.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.663
I'm surprised you haven't noticed that.

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:58.240
- Sorry you got fired, here's a latte.

00:05:58.240 --> 00:05:59.400
- Oh, uh.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:00.260
- It's decaf ma'am.

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:01.590
- Thanks Judah.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.730
You know, one year ago a setback like this

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:06.450
would have really spun me out,
but I don't need Courtney.

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:08.420
Every time we fall, we get back up

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:09.880
stronger and better than ever.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:11.400
Can I get a hallelujah?

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:12.680
- Is that a sort of press juice?

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:14.870
I'll have one hallelujah
on your desk by 12:45.

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:15.703
- Great.

00:06:15.703 --> 00:06:16.536
What's next?

00:06:16.536 --> 00:06:17.410
- I noticed your necklace was broken,

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:18.920
so I push back your doctor's appointment

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:20.480
and found a reputable jeweler nearby.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:23.090
- Don't know what I'd do
without you my harry number two.

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:25.170
Oh god, I'm sorry that came out horribly.

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:27.330
- Not to speak above
my station, but perhaps

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:29.350
it would behoove us to
entice BoJack Horseman

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:30.262
back into our stable.

00:06:30.262 --> 00:06:31.095
- Ugh.

00:06:31.095 --> 00:06:33.630
I'm sorry ma'am, stable and
behoove were poor word choices.

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:35.820
I was not trying to engage in
punery during business hours

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:38.060
but we've received 15 more inquiries

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:39.620
about BoJack just this morning.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:42.040
And I don't think it's
wise to look at gift,

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:43.457
opportunity in the mouth.

00:06:43.457 --> 00:06:45.390
- BoJack is off the table.

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:47.020
We're a small management company.

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:49.038
We just need to focus
on the clients we have.

00:06:49.038 --> 00:06:49.871
- You know best.

00:06:49.871 --> 00:06:51.150
Oh, excuse me, hello.

00:06:51.150 --> 00:06:54.650
- Judah, you'll never
guess who I just ran into.

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:55.483
- No, I won't.

00:06:55.483 --> 00:06:56.390
Very astute, ma'am.

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.993
- It was Charlie Witherspoon.

00:06:58.993 --> 00:06:59.826
- Uh huh.
(ominous music)

00:06:59.826 --> 00:07:04.000
- Char-Lee Wither-Spoon.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:04.833
- Okay.

00:07:04.833 --> 00:07:06.760
- How does that make you feel?

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:08.490
- That very short story
makes me feel nothing.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.460
But I don't think it's your
fault as a storyteller.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:12.990
I often have trouble
engaging with narratives.

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.700
Oh, I didn't realize you were still here.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.180
Do you need anything else before I go?

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:18.010
- No, thank you.

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:19.470
- Should you be drinking that?

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:21.640
- You don't always know
what's best for me, Judah.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:23.240
- Is everything okay Princess Caroline?

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:26.730
- Charlie Witherspoon made
you an offer to buy them

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:29.160
and you went over my
head and turned them down

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:30.620
without telling me.

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:31.453
- Oh.

00:07:31.453 --> 00:07:33.150
- So it's true, you lied to me.

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:33.983
- Yes.

00:07:33.983 --> 00:07:35.640
- Because you didn't want
to work in a big agency.

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.590
You don't fit in with other people.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:38.630
You're weird.

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:41.460
So you'd rather stay here
where you have all the power.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:42.293
- No Princess Caroline.

00:07:42.293 --> 00:07:44.780
- So you lied to me and you
made me look like an idiot.

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:46.200
- I was trying to protect you.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.230
I knew if you heard the offer,

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:48.430
you'd feel like you have to say yes.

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:49.263
- I don't need you to protect me.

00:07:49.263 --> 00:07:50.360
- But if you had more time,

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.840
you could decide what
you wanted to do next

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:53.500
on your own terms, which you did.

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:55.170
- Well, that's not your decision to make.

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:57.110
- Princess Caroline, I
understand you're upset,

00:07:57.110 --> 00:07:57.954
and perhaps your emotion--

00:07:57.954 --> 00:07:58.787
- No.

00:07:58.787 --> 00:08:01.520
If I can't trust you, then
I can't work with you.

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:02.353
You're fired.

00:08:03.837 --> 00:08:06.340
(heavy sighing)

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:08.170
- Thank you for my time
here Princess Caroline.

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:09.680
It's been very pleasurable.

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:13.223
Until now, this part is sad.

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:17.060
Don't forget to have
reservations at eight.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:17.990
- Thank you, Judah.

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:18.823
- Good night.

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:22.390
- These strike negotiations
have lasted so long,

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:24.130
it's like Red's in this board room.

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:24.963
Remember Red's?

00:08:24.963 --> 00:08:27.190
Two VHS tapes, that's
too many tapes, I said.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:29.740
But no one listens to Lenny.

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:30.960
- How's this look?

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:32.790
- Generous, but you're
making up the projected loss

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:34.650
by excising office birthday cakes.

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:35.810
That's unacceptable.

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:37.800
- Everybody hates office parties.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:39.610
- Everyone hates the
mysterious dried fruit cubes

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:40.940
in trail mix, but we still eat them

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:42.350
after the other nuts and seeds are gone

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:45.020
because in our undervalued
overworked existence,

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:47.050
we're desperate for any
morsel of satisfaction

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:49.650
whether that be cake,
unidentifiable orange fruit shards,

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:51.620
or the occasional kind word from our boss.

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:52.453
- I like cake.

00:08:52.453 --> 00:08:53.990
They can print those pictures on them now.

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:54.990
What's the issue here?

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:56.930
- Fine, but we're grouping birthdays

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:58.530
so they only happen once a month.

00:08:58.530 --> 00:08:59.730
- We accept those terms.

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:01.360
We're left with one final issue.

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:04.740
- Your insistence assistants
be not treated like garbage.

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:07.660
From this day forth, all
assistants will be treated

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:10.470
like recycling right next to the garbage,

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:12.180
but with an understanding that one day

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:15.070
they may be upcycled to a higher status.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:17.560
Oh, like a bunch of seat belts
that got turned into a purse

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:19.820
or a license plate that
gets turned into a purse,

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:20.653
right Lenny?

00:09:20.653 --> 00:09:22.220
- Sure, sure, I'm green.

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:24.074
We're amenable to these terms.

00:09:24.074 --> 00:09:26.824
(ethereal music)

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:31.030
- Judah, I meant to reach out.

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:32.140
- There's no need to explain.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:33.760
I know you're very busy
with work and Ruthie.

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:35.500
- Ha, you have no idea.

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:36.800
- I have some idea.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:39.060
You talked about it quite
often during the negotiations.

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:40.730
- This strike has been the most time

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:42.606
I've been able to spend with Ruthie since,

00:09:42.606 --> 00:09:44.410
(baby garbles)
ever.

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:46.760
- I also feel an ambivalence
about the strike ending.

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:48.780
The negotiations have
been quite invigorating.

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:51.290
- And now you're just gonna
ride off into the sunset?

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:53.430
- No the sun sets in the west.

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:56.030
I'm riding east to my Atwater cottage.

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:56.863
Goodbye.

00:09:56.863 --> 00:09:57.696
- Judah?

00:09:57.696 --> 00:09:58.529
- Yes?

00:09:58.529 --> 00:10:00.810
- You're the best assistant I ever had.

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:03.460
- You don't need ever in
that sentence, it's implied.

00:10:05.178 --> 00:10:08.858
(light music)
(sighing)

00:10:08.858 --> 00:10:09.691
(knocking)

00:10:09.691 --> 00:10:10.600
- Come in.

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:11.433
- Pardon my state.

00:10:11.433 --> 00:10:13.040
I was mid trek of a Los Angeles crest

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:14.030
when I received your text.

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:15.000
You had a question for me?

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:15.833
- Yes.

00:10:15.833 --> 00:10:18.540
Would you be interested in
interviewing for a job here

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:20.410
as VIM's Chief of Operations?

00:10:20.410 --> 00:10:22.560
You'd be a partner with
a stake in the company,

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:24.230
and a birthday cake just for you.

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:26.050
- I would be interested in that interview.

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:26.930
- Do you want the job?

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:27.763
- Yes.

00:10:27.763 --> 00:10:28.700
Great, interview done.

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:30.660
Your first task is to clear my schedule

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:31.750
every third Friday.

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:33.500
I'm taking them off to
be with my daughter.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:35.830
And there's a weird burnt smell
coming from the copy room.

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:36.940
- I'm familiar with that smell.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:38.670
I'll investigate right away.

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:40.240
- Thanks Judah.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:41.211
- My pleasure.

00:10:41.211 --> 00:10:44.294
(light guitar music)

